user_prompt:
Variables are listed below in random order. Use the exact id strings.
[
  {
    "id": "smoking"
  },
  {
    "id": "bronchitis"
  },
  {
    "id": "dyspnoea"
  },
  {
    "id": "tuberculosis"
  },
  {
    "id": "lung cancer"
  },
  {
    "id": "positive X-ray"
  },
  {
    "id": "visit to Asia"
  }
]

Task: propose a causal order prior. Earlier variables are potential causes or upstream conditions; later variables are downstream effects, measurements, symptoms, decisions, or aggregate outcomes.

Return one JSON object with this schema:
{
  "ordered_nodes": ["exact id 1", "exact id 2", "..."],
  "confidence": 0.0,
  "high_confidence_pairs": [
    {"before": "exact id", "after": "exact id", "confidence": 0.0}
  ],
  "rationale": "brief, no more than 80 words"
}

Constraints: ordered_nodes must contain every provided id exactly once; do not invent nodes; if evidence is weak, still provide the best semantic prior and lower the confidence.

raw_response:
{
  "ordered_nodes": ["visit to Asia", "smoking", "tuberculosis", "lung cancer", "bronchitis", "dyspnoea", "positive X-ray"],
  "confidence": 0.84,
  "high_confidence_pairs": [
    {"before": "visit to Asia", "after": "tuberculosis", "confidence": 0.97},
    {"before": "smoking", "after": "lung cancer", "confidence": 0.95},
    {"before": "smoking", "after": "bronchitis", "confidence": 0.94},
    {"before": "tuberculosis", "after": "positive X-ray", "confidence": 0.93},
    {"before": "lung cancer", "after": "dyspnoea", "confidence": 0.84},
    {"before": "bronchitis", "after": "dyspnoea", "confidence": 0.8}
  ],
  "rationale": "Travel to Asia can increase tuberculosis risk; smoking is an upstream exposure for lung cancer and bronchitis. Tuberculosis, lung cancer, and bronchitis can cause dyspnoea, while positive X-ray is typically a downstream diagnostic finding after disease onset. Exact temporal ordering among the diseases is uncertain, so this is a semantic prior only."
}
